│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ compressed_ring_crz_entangler                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current seed block uses 24 continuous parameters per candidate block (8×RY + 8×RZ +   │
│                          │ 8×RZ), leading to 146 total trainable parameters across the fixed re-uploading structure  │
│                          │ (3 uploads × 2 repeats + 2 readout calibration params). Although accuracy is strong,      │
│                          │ parameter efficiency is poor.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This rewrite keeps the same overall fixed training loop, feature map, re-uploading (l=3)  │
│                          │ and ansatz application frequency (p=2), and the same readout (mean Z with gain/bias).     │
│                          │ Only ANSATZ_SPEC is changed.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Reduce ansatz parameters per block from 24 → 20 by replacing the “pre RZ + post RZ”     │
│                          │ double layer (16 params) with a single RZ layer (8 params).                               │
│                          │ - Add a small number (4) of parametrized controlled-Z rotations (CRZ) to restore          │
│                          │ expressive entangling power with fewer parameters.                                        │
│                          │ - Use a ring-like, non-linear CZ entangling pattern on additional qubit pairs to          │
│                          │ complement the dataset’s feature-map couplings.                                           │
│                          │ - Overall effect: lower L2 loss via better inductive bias, reduced train-test gap by      │
│                          │ controlling over-parameterization, and improved parameter efficiency (fewer trainable     │
│                          │ circuit parameters).                                                                      │
