│ patch_name               │ entangled_feature_diffusion                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The previous linear-chain approach lacked sufficient expressive power to capture complex  │
│                          │ correlations between the 28 binary features. This new implementation adopts a 'diffusive' │
│                          │ entanglement strategy using a circular topology (ring) of parametric CRZ gates. By        │
│                          │ connecting qubit `i` to `i+1` (and `7` to `0`), we create a hardware-efficient            │
│                          │ 'brick-wall' style connectivity that allows information to propagate across the entire    │
│                          │ register within a single ansatz block. This design significantly improves the circuit's   │
│                          │ ability to model high-order correlations while remaining within the parameter budget.     │
