│                          │ entanglement could be improved by using a more connected entanglement pattern that better │
│                          │ utilizes the 8-qubit system. Additionally, we can add more expressivity by including both │
│                          │ RX and RY rotations in the local rotation layers, which can help break symmetry and       │
│                          │ improve learning capacity.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The changes include:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Replacing the ring CZ structure with a more connected pattern that creates more        │
│                          │ entanglement pathways                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. Adding RX rotations alongside RY rotations in the input layer to increase expressivity │
│                          │ 3. Adding a second layer of local rotations (RY) before the entangling gates to enhance   │
│                          │ state preparation                                                                         │
│                          │ 4. Keeping the CRZ gates for parameterized entanglement                                   │
│                          │ 5. Maintaining the output RZ layer for final phase adjustments                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach should improve the circuit's ability to learn complex patterns in the data  │
│                          │ while maintaining a reasonable parameter count.                                           │
