│ patch_description        │ Replace the final post single-qubit RZ layer with an adaptive, parameterized entangling   │
│                          │ layer using CRZ gates.                                                                    │
│                          │ We keep the current parameter budget per block (12 unique parameters) by:                 │
│                          │ - Keeping the pairwise-shared RY parameters (4 params).                                   │
│                          │ - Keeping the pairwise-shared pre-RZ parameters (4 params).                               │
│                          │ - Adding 4 new pairwise-shared CRZ parameters (4 params).                                 │
│                          │ - Removing the 4 pairwise-shared post-RZ parameters (8 RZ gates).                         │
│                          │ This increases expressivity (adaptive phase entanglement) while maintaining the same      │
│                          │ number of circuit parameters, which should improve validation/test accuracy and reduce    │
│                          │ the train-test gap.                                                                       │
