│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sharedrzcrzring_v2_globalz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This new ansatz block keeps the same overall training pipeline and feature map, but       │
│                          │ changes the variational structure to be more parameter-efficient and less prone to        │
│                          │ train-test mismatch. Concretely: it (1) uses strong parameter sharing for all             │
│                          │ single-qubit rotations (only 6–8 unique parameters per block), (2) uses a fixed CZ ring   │
│                          │ pattern for entanglement (no extra parameters), (3) adds a single shared CRZ parameter on │
│                          │ a set of paired edges to introduce controlled nonlinearity, and (4) adds a global         │
│                          │ trainable RZ “phase-tuning” parameter at the end of the block to stabilize optimization   │
│                          │ and improve calibration without increasing expressivity too much.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
