╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ interleaved_rings_crossover                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of both programs to create a more efficient      │
│                          │ ansatz. It takes the proven interleaved CZ ring structure from the first program (which   │
│                          │ showed excellent convergence at step 150) and combines it with the parameter-efficient    │
│                          │ coarse-grained parameter sharing from the second program. The key improvements are:       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Maintains the interleaved CZ rings structure that demonstrated faster convergence (150 │
│                          │ vs 270 steps)                                                                             │
│                          │ 2. Uses coarse-grained parameter sharing (4 parameters instead of 8) to reduce total      │
│                          │ parameter count from 74 to 38                                                             │
│                          │ 3. Keeps the additional chord entanglement (CZ gates between opposite qubits) for better  │
│                          │ expressivity                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. Preserves the pre/post RZ layer structure for better optimization landscape            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
