│ patch_name               │ hierarchical_parameter_sharing                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation introduces hierarchical parameter sharing to reduce the total number  │
│                          │ of parameters while maintaining model expressivity. The key changes are:                  │
│                          │ 1. Grouping qubits into 4 pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) for coarse-grained parameter sharing │
│                          │ 2. Using upload-indexed parameter names (e.g., "ry_u0", "ry_u1", "ry_u2") to share        │
│                          │ parameters across repeats within each upload                                              │
│                          │ 3. Maintaining the same entanglement structure with CZ rings and ladders                  │
│                          │ 4. Reducing total parameters from 74 to 38 (40% reduction) which improves parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency                                                                                │
│                          │ 5. Preserving the original N_UPLOADS=3 and N_REPEATS=2 configuration for fair comparison  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach should reduce overfitting, improve generalization gap, and increase         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency while maintaining high accuracy.                                     │
