│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crz_ansatz                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover approach improves upon the previous coarse-grained architecture by         │
│                          │ introducing adaptive, parameter-shared entangling gates (CRZ) while maintaining the same  │
│                          │ low parameter count.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By replacing the static pre-entanglement rotation layer with a CRZ layer (shared across   │
│                          │ the two qubit banks: 0-3 and 4-7), we increase the circuit's ability to model complex     │
│                          │ dependencies between the features and the qubit states. The proven interleaved CZ-ring    │
│                          │ structure is retained for fixed global entanglement. This configuration keeps the         │
│                          │ parameter budget tight to prevent overfitting while offering a more expressive            │
│                          │ variational space compared to the previous purely rotational-based ansatz.                │
