│ patch_description        │ I am upgrading the ansatz to use a "SU(2) rotation sequence" (RX, RY, RZ) on each qubit,  │
│                          │ which significantly enhances the circuit's expressivity compared to the previous          │
│                          │ RY-RZ-only setup. To keep the parameter count manageable and prevent overfitting (as      │
│                          │ evidenced by the low generalization gap requirement), I continue using coarse-grained     │
│                          │ parameter sharing across the two halves of the register (qubits 0-3 and 4-7). I maintain  │
│                          │ the highly effective interleaved CZ ring entanglement structure combined with inter-group │
│                          │ cross-chords, which ensures consistent global entanglement across all uploads. This       │
│                          │ configuration increases the per-block parameter count to 8, leading to a total of 50      │
│                          │ circuit parameters, striking a better balance between expressivity and optimization       │
│                          │ stability.                                                                                │
