│ patch_name               │ parameter_efficient_cry_ansatz                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This modification aims to improve the parameter efficiency while maintaining expressivity │
│                          │ by reducing the number of trainable CRY gates and optimizing parameter sharing. The       │
│                          │ previous version had too many independent CRY parameters (8), which increased the total   │
│                          │ parameter count significantly without proportional performance gains. This version        │
│                          │ reduces CRY gates and shares parameters more effectively across qubit pairs while         │
│                          │ maintaining the entangling capability.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Reduce CRY gates from 8 to 4 by pairing them more effectively                          │
│                          │ 2. Share CRY parameters between symmetric qubit pairs to reduce parameter count           │
│                          │ 3. Maintain the CZ ring structure that showed good performance in previous iterations     │
│                          │ 4. Keep the coarse-grained RY and RZ parameter sharing that proved effective              │
