│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ banked_rx_rz_cz_shared                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Improves the ansatz by:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Keeping parameter efficiency while adding expressivity: introduces one shared RX        │
│                          │ rotation (single parameter) in addition to the proven 2-bank shared RY and 2-bank shared  │
│                          │ RZ parameters.                                                                            │
│                          │ - Avoids extra parameter growth by reusing the same RZ parameters for both the “pre” and  │
│                          │ “post” RZ layers (within the same ansatz block), and reuses the same two-bank RY          │
│                          │ parameters everywhere.                                                                    │
│                          │ - Preserves the high-performing entangling pattern (two interleaved CZ rings plus         │
│                          │ opposite-chord CZs) and keeps all wiring/allowed-gate constraints valid.                  │
│                          │ Net effect: reduces parameters from 38 to 32 (per circuit it is still consistent with the │
│                          │ fixed training pipeline), while increasing representational power for faster convergence  │
│                          │ and better validation/test accuracy.                                                      │
