│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fine_grained_four_bank_classifier                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This design refines the parameter sharing strategy by dividing the 8 qubits into four     │
│                          │ 2-qubit sub-banks ([0,1], [2,3], [4,5], [6,7]) instead of two 4-qubit banks. This allows  │
│                          │ for more granular control while maintaining parameter efficiency. Key innovations         │
│                          │ include:                                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. Separate RY and RZ parameters for each sub-bank to improve expressivity                │
│                          │ 2. Strategic use of CRZ gates between sub-banks to enhance inter-block communication      │
│                          │ 3. Maintained CZ ring structure for local entanglement                                    │
│                          │ 4. Reduced parameter count (48 vs 62) while increasing model capacity                     │
│                          │ 5. Better balance between expressivity and generalization to reduce overfitting           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The approach draws from the previous coarse-grained designs but increases granularity to  │
│                          │ better capture local correlations in the feature space, while using controlled rotations  │
│                          │ to maintain global coherence.                                                             │
