│ patch_description        │ This edit streamlines the ansatz block to improve training efficiency and performance,    │
│                          │ based on the recommendation to use learnable CRZ chords. Specifically:                    │
│                          │ 1. Removes the redundant "RX" rotation layer, which contributed significant parameters    │
│                          │ but likely limited expressivity.                                                          │
│                          │ 2. Removes the "Global RZ" layer, as it was redundant with local post-rotations.          │
│                          │ 3. Implements the recommendation: replaces the fixed CZ chords with learnable CRZ chords  │
│                          │ using a single shared parameter `crz_chord`.                                              │
│                          │ 4. Retains the essential "interleaved rings" entanglement and the local RY/RZ structures. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the parameter count per block from 10 to 8, leading to better optimization   │
│                          │ behavior (lower `n_params` overall), consistent with the successful seed architecture's   │
