│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best features from both parent programs to create a more      │
│                          │ efficient ansatz. The key improvements are:                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Parameter efficiency: Reduced from 74 to 26 parameters by using coarse-grained         │
│                          │ parameter sharing (similar to the high-performing parent)                                 │
│                          │ 2. Learnable entanglement: Replaced fixed CZ gates with parametrized CRZ gates to         │
│                          │ increase expressivity while maintaining parameter efficiency                              │
│                          │ 3. Structured entanglement: Maintained the ring and chord entanglement structure but made │
│                          │ it learnable                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. Bank-based sharing: Kept the efficient two-bank (0-3 vs 4-7) parameter sharing scheme  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The design keeps the essential structure of the better-performing parent                  │
│                          │ (parameter-efficient coarse-grained sharing) while incorporating the learnable            │
│                          │ entanglement concept. This results in a circuit that achieves higher accuracy with        │
│                          │ significantly fewer parameters, improving parameter efficiency and reducing overfitting   │
│                          │ potential.                                                                                │
