│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ cz_ring_chord_rzry_shared_4param                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the current ansatz block with a more parameter-efficient 4-parameter design by:  │
│                          │ - Using a single shared RZ parameter across all qubits for both the pre- and              │
│                          │ post-entanglement layers (same param key reused).                                         │
│                          │ - Keeping only two shared RY parameters for the (0–3) and (4–7) qubit banks.              │
│                          │ - Using just two shared CRZ strength parameters: one for the interleaved ring pattern and │
│                          │ one for the opposite chords.                                                              │
│                          │ - Reordering the internal block to RZ_pre → CRZ(entangle) → RY → RZ_post to improve       │
│                          │ information flow while keeping the same overall circuit wiring/depth pattern.             │
│                          │ This reduces N_PARAMS (per block) substantially while maintaining strong expressivity via │
│                          │ the CRZ entangling structure.                                                             │
