│ patch_name               │ hierarchical_ry_offset_parameters                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This change introduces hierarchical single-qubit offset parameters to enhance the         │
│                          │ expressivity of the ansatz while maintaining parameter efficiency. By adding small        │
│                          │ per-block offset keys ("Δry_h" and "Δry_h2") to the existing "ry_h" and "ry_h2"           │
│                          │ parameters, we allow each block to locally adjust its rotation bias. This approach        │
│                          │ preserves the coarse-grained parameter sharing between the two 4-qubit banks (0-3 and     │
│                          │ 4-7) while providing more flexibility in the rotations. The hierarchical scheme should    │
│                          │ help lift performance without significantly increasing the parameter count or risking     │
│                          │ overfitting.                                                                              │
