│ patch_name               │ ring_chord_crz_rzpre_rypost_rzpost                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Redesigns the EVOLVE-BLOCK ansatz ordering for better information flow and trainability:  │
│                          │ - Uses shared RZ “pre” rotations on two banks (qubits 0–3 vs 4–7).                        │
│                          │ - Applies trainable CRZ entanglers (ring + opposite-chord) with only two shared           │
│                          │ parameters (chi_ring, chi_chord) to keep parameter efficiency high.                       │
│                          │ - Moves the shared RY layer to *after* entanglement (RY “post”), then finishes with a     │
│                          │ shared RZ “post” layer.                                                                   │
│                          │ This implements the suggested RZ_pre → CRZ entanglers → RY → RZ_post structure to improve │
│                          │ convergence and generalization while keeping the fixed training/feature map/measurement   │
│                          │ pipeline unchanged.                                                                       │
